TASK SPECIFICATIONS:
{
  "id": "PUB005",
  "title": "Weld Gap Alarm and Startup Inhibition",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "requirements": "# Weld Gap Alarm and Startup Inhibition\n\n- **Difficulty:** Easy (easy)\n\n## Requirements\n\nControl a weld-gap alarm with power-up monitoring inhibition, input debouncing during normal monitoring and emergency-stop priority.\n\n1. Gap_Exceeded indicates that the scanner has detected a weld gap exceeding the permitted 1.5 mm value.\n2. Begin with a 5-second initialization inhibition period after power-up. During this period, Operator_Alert is FALSE, Weld_Soft_Start_Active is TRUE, and gap-signal debounce time does not accumulate.\n3. Resume gap monitoring after initialization. Allow the alarm only after Gap_Exceeded has remained TRUE for DebounceTime. When the signal becomes FALSE, switch off the alarm and clear debounce timing.\n4. When Weld_E_Stop_NC is FALSE, the emergency stop takes priority over initialization and normal monitoring. Operator_Alert must immediately become FALSE and any incomplete debounce timing must be cleared.\n5. Weld_Soft_Start_Active indicates only the power-up inhibition period; it does not represent a continuous speed ramp.\n\n## Interface Definition\n\n| Direction | Variable/Field | Data Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Input | `Gap_Exceeded` | `BOOL` | Scanner indication that the gap exceeds 1.5 mm. |\n| Input | `Weld_E_Stop_NC` | `BOOL` | TRUE means the emergency stop is inactive; FALSE means it is active. |\n| Input | `DebounceTime` | `TIME` | Gap-signal debounce duration during normal monitoring; must be positive. |\n| Output | `Operator_Alert` | `BOOL` | Audible and visual alarm command. |\n| Output | `Weld_Soft_Start_Active` | `BOOL` | Monitoring-inhibition status during the 5-second power-up initialization. |",
  "scenario": "Control a weld-gap alarm with power-up monitoring inhibition, input debouncing during normal monitoring and emergency-stop priority.",
  "interface": [
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "Gap_Exceeded",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Scanner indication that the gap exceeds 1.5 mm."
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "Weld_E_Stop_NC",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "TRUE means the emergency stop is inactive; FALSE means it is active."
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "DebounceTime",
      "type": "TIME",
      "description": "Gap-signal debounce duration during normal monitoring; must be positive."
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "Operator_Alert",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Audible and visual alarm command."
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "Weld_Soft_Start_Active",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Monitoring-inhibition status during the 5-second power-up initialization."
    }
  ],
  "initial_conditions": {
    "Operator_Alert": false,
    "Weld_Soft_Start_Active": true,
    "startupElapsed_ms": 0,
    "gapElapsed_ms": 0
  },
  "scan_semantics": "At scan k, inputs I[k] are sampled once, q[k] is pre-scan retained state, outputs O[k] are observed after execution, and q[k+1] is the updated state. Each test creates a fresh FB instance before step 0. An initialized instance has not yet executed a scan. Timer elapsed time is zero on the first eligible sampled invocation; dt_ms is elapsed wall time since the previous invocation, not automatically a synthetic input to the FB. No unobserved past input stability is assumed. All sequences here are expected values.",
  "safety_priority": [
    "E-stop immediately suppresses the alarm in every phase.",
    "Initialization suppresses alarm and prevents gap timing."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Power-up inhibition uses a monotonically advancing 5-second timer that starts on the first FB invocation and continues through E-stop.",
    "Weld_Soft_Start_Active reports startup inhibition even during E-stop. E-stop overrides the alert and resets gap timing but does not restart power-up inhibition.",
    "At exactly 5 seconds startup inhibition clears. That scan is the first eligible gap sample, with gap elapsed zero; there is no credited debounce time during inhibition.",
    "DebounceTime is positive. Alert clears and debounce resets immediately on raw gap FALSE or E-stop.",
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values.",
    "DebounceTime is a strictly positive constant throughout each test case. Dynamic changes are outside this benchmark domain. Time must advance for eventual-start properties.",
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values."
  ],
  "ltl": [
    {
      "id": "PUB005.P_init",
      "kind": "safety",
      "formula": "init",
      "description": "Before the first scan invocation, all declared OUTPUT variables and initial instance state hold their declared initial values.",
      "explanation": "Applies strictly to the fresh pre-invocation initial instance observation before scan k=0 (INITIAL_INSTANCE scope).",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "INITIAL_INSTANCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB005.P1",
      "formula": "G(Weld_Soft_Start_Active <-> startup)",
      "explanation": "Soft-start output means only the startup monitoring inhibition interval.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB005.P2",
      "formula": "G((startup | !Weld_E_Stop_NC | !Gap_Exceeded) -> !Operator_Alert)",
      "explanation": "Startup, E-stop or no gap forces the alarm off.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB005.P3",
      "formula": "G(Operator_Alert <-> (!startup & Weld_E_Stop_NC & Gap_Exceeded & gapQualified))",
      "explanation": "Alarm requires post-startup continuous qualified gap.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB005.P4",
      "formula": "G((startup | !Weld_E_Stop_NC | !Gap_Exceeded) -> X(!gapQualified))",
      "explanation": "Each suppressing condition clears or blocks gap qualification.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB005.P5",
      "formula": "(G(F(TimeTick))) -> (G((G(Weld_E_Stop_NC & Gap_Exceeded)) -> F(Operator_Alert)))",
      "explanation": "Persistent gap eventually alarms after startup and debounce, assuming advancing time. Explicit non-Zeno environment premise: physical elapsed time crosses infinitely many 1ms boundaries.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    }
  ],
  "atomic_propositions": {
    "startup": "Elapsed time since the first invocation is less than 5 seconds.",
    "gapQualified": "Gap_Exceeded has remained TRUE with Weld_E_Stop_NC TRUE and !startup for at least DebounceTime, measured from first eligible invocation.",
    "interface names": "Identically named sampled input or observed output.",
    "TimeTick": "Boolean: floor(t[k]/1ms)>floor(t[k-1]/1ms), with t[0]=0, TimeTick[0]=FALSE, t[k]=sum(dt_ms[1..k]). G(F(TimeTick)) states unbounded physical time progress; merely positive dt is insufficient.",
    "Gap_Exceeded": "I[k].Gap_Exceeded: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "Weld_E_Stop_NC": "I[k].Weld_E_Stop_NC: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "DebounceTime": "I[k].DebounceTime: sampled input (TIME).",
    "Operator_Alert": "O[k].Operator_Alert: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "Weld_Soft_Start_Active": "O[k].Weld_Soft_Start_Active: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "init": "At the separate pre-invocation initial observation before scan k=0: O_init.Operator_Alert=false, O_init.Weld_Soft_Start_Active=true."
  }
}

ARCHITECTURAL PLAN:
{
  "state_machine": {
    "states": [
      {
        "name": "S_INITIALIZING",
        "description": "Power-up monitoring inhibition active. Weld_Soft_Start_Active is TRUE. Operator_Alert is forced FALSE. Gap debounce timing is inhibited/reset."
      },
      {
        "name": "S_MONITORING",
        "description": "Post-startup normal monitoring. Gap_Exceeded may qualify after continuous DebounceTime when E-stop is inactive. Weld_Soft_Start_Active is FALSE."
      }
    ],
    "transitions": [
      {
        "from": "S_INITIALIZING",
        "to": "S_MONITORING",
        "guard": "StartupTimer.Q == TRUE, i.e. startupActive == FALSE. State is supervisory; functional gating uses post-stage-3 startupActive derived from StartupTimer.Q."
      },
      {
        "from": "S_MONITORING",
        "to": "S_MONITORING",
        "guard": "StartupTimer.Q == TRUE; no return to initialization without power cycle/fresh FB instance."
      },
      {
        "from": "ANY_STATE",
        "to": "SAME_STATE",
        "guard": "Weld_E_Stop_NC == FALSE: E-stop priority override. Operator_Alert := FALSE; GapDebounceTimer reset. StartupTimer continues; Weld_Soft_Start_Active remains startupActive, so it can still be TRUE during E-stop if within the 5 s startup interval."
      },
      {
        "from": "S_MONITORING",
        "to": "S_MONITORING",
        "guard": "Gap_Exceeded == FALSE: Operator_Alert := FALSE and GapDebounceTimer reset."
      },
      {
        "from": "S_MONITORING",
        "to": "S_MONITORING",
        "guard": "startupActive == FALSE AND Weld_E_Stop_NC == TRUE AND Gap_Exceeded == TRUE AND GapDebounceTimer.Q == TRUE: Operator_Alert := TRUE."
      }
    ]
  },
  "timer_plan": [
    {
      "name": "StartupTimer",
      "type": "TON",
      "PT": "T#5s",
      "IN": "TRUE after first FB invocation; remains TRUE through E-stop, gap changes, and state changes.",
      "reset_conditions": "Fresh FB instance/power-up only. Not reset by Weld_E_Stop_NC, Gap_Exceeded, or state transition.",
      "use": "StartupTimer.Q == TRUE means the 5 s initialization inhibition has completed. startupActive := NOT StartupTimer.Q. Weld_Soft_Start_Active := startupActive."
    },
    {
      "name": "GapDebounceTimer",
      "type": "TON",
      "PT": "DebounceTime, sampled each scan; assumed strictly positive.",
      "IN": "NOT startupActive AND Weld_E_Stop_NC AND Gap_Exceeded, evaluated after the unconditional StartupTimer call in stage 3.",
      "reset_conditions": "IN == FALSE: resets ET to zero and Q to FALSE. This occurs during startup, on E-stop active, or when Gap_Exceeded is FALSE. Also reset on fresh FB/power-up.",
      "use": "GapDebounceTimer.Q is TRUE only after Gap_Exceeded has remained TRUE continuously for DebounceTime while post-startup and E-stop inactive. At the exact scan startup clears, the first eligible gap invocation has ET = 0 and no debounce time is credited from the inhibition period."
    }
  ],
  "priorities": [
    "1. E-stop highest priority: Weld_E_Stop_NC == FALSE forces Operator_Alert := FALSE immediately and resets GapDebounceTimer. E-stop does not restart or reset StartupTimer, and does not change Weld_Soft_Start_Active except as determined by the continuing startup timer.",
    "2. Power-up initialization priority: while startupActive == TRUE, Operator_Alert is forced FALSE, Weld_Soft_Start_Active is TRUE, and GapDebounceTimer is inhibited/reset.",
    "3. Raw gap FALSE reset: Gap_Exceeded == FALSE forces Operator_Alert := FALSE and resets GapDebounceTimer immediately.",
    "4. Normal qualified-gap alarm: Operator_Alert may be TRUE only when startupActive == FALSE, Weld_E_Stop_NC == TRUE, Gap_Exceeded == TRUE, and GapDebounceTimer.Q == TRUE.",
    "5. Deterministic output stage: outputs are assigned once in stage 4 after safety, state, and timer execution."
  ],
  "initial_values": {
    "Operator_Alert": false,
    "Weld_Soft_Start_Active": true,
    "state": "S_INITIALIZING",
    "startupActive": true,
    "gapQualified": false,
    "firstScan": true,
    "StartupTimer.IN": true,
    "StartupTimer.PT": "T#5s",
    "StartupTimer.ET": "T#0s",
    "StartupTimer.Q": false,
    "GapDebounceTimer.IN": false,
    "GapDebounceTimer.PT_source": "DebounceTime",
    "GapDebounceTimer.ET": "T#0s",
    "GapDebounceTimer.Q": false,
    "startupElapsed_ms": 0,
    "gapElapsed_ms": 0
  },
  "scan_execution_order": [
    "Stage 1 - Edge sampling: sample Gap_Exceeded, Weld_E_Stop_NC, and DebounceTime once per scan. Latch firstScan if needed for FB initialization; no hidden input-stability assumptions are used.",
    "Stage 2 - Safety/reset priority and state transitions: evaluate E-stop first, then startup inhibition, then raw Gap_Exceeded FALSE reset. Set supervisory state transition requests using prior retained timer/state information; final functional startupActive is recomputed after the unconditional StartupTimer call.",
    "Stage 3 - Unconditional top-level timer FB calls outside CASE/IF: call StartupTimer(IN := TRUE, PT := T#5s); update startupActive := NOT StartupTimer.Q; set GapDebounceTimer.PT := DebounceTime; call GapDebounceTimer(IN := NOT startupActive AND Weld_E_Stop_NC AND Gap_Exceeded, PT := DebounceTime).",
    "Stage 4 - Unified output assignments: Operator_Alert := (NOT startupActive) AND Weld_E_Stop_NC AND Gap_Exceeded AND GapDebounceTimer.Q; Weld_Soft_Start_Active := startupActive. No other output assignments occur."
  ],
  "formal_assertions": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "formula": "G(!Weld_E_Stop_NC -> !Operator_Alert)"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "formula": "G(Weld_Soft_Start_Active -> !Operator_Alert)"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "formula": "G(!Gap_Exceeded -> !Operator_Alert)"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "formula": "G(Operator_Alert -> (Weld_E_Stop_NC AND Gap_Exceeded AND !Weld_Soft_Start_Active))"
    }
  ]
}

CODESYS DIALECT CARDS:
[
  {
    "id": "ton_timer",
    "title": "Standard IEC TON Timer Block Invocation",
    "body": "// Standard IEC TON timer: MUST invoke unconditionally OUTSIDE CASE/IF every scan!\nVAR\n    timer : TON;\n    runTimer : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\n// Control via boolean IN flag (never put timer(...) only inside an IF/CASE arm):\nrunTimer := (state = 1) AND NOT resetCmd;\ntimer(IN := runTimer, PT := T#2s);\nIF timer.Q THEN\n    // Timer expired; timer.ET holds elapsed time\nEND_IF;"
  },
  {
    "id": "case_state_machine",
    "title": "Explicit CASE State Machine Transitions",
    "body": "// 4-Stage Scan Order: 1) Edge sample 2) Reset/priority & CASE state transition\n// 3) Unconditional top-level TON/R_TRIG calls 4) Unified output assignments\nVAR\n    state : INT := 0; // 0=IDLE, 1=RUN, 2=FAULT\nEND_VAR\nIF emergencyStop THEN state := 2; END_IF;\nCASE state OF\n    0: IF startCmd AND NOT fault THEN state := 1; END_IF;\n    1: IF faultCmd THEN state := 2; ELSIF stopCmd THEN state := 0; END_IF;\n    2: IF resetCmd THEN state := 0; END_IF;\n    ELSE state := 0;\nEND_CASE;\noutActive := (state = 1); // Assign outputs unconditionally from current state"
  },
  {
    "id": "ltime_ops",
    "title": "LTIME and TIME Literals and Operations",
    "body": "// TIME (T#... 32-bit) and LTIME (LTIME#... 64-bit nanosecond) literals & ops\nVAR\n    tCycle : TIME := T#100ms;\n    ltAcc : LTIME := LTIME#0ms;\n    ltLimit : LTIME := LTIME#10s;\nEND_VAR\nltAcc := ltAcc + LTIME#100ms;\nIF ltAcc >= ltLimit THEN\n    ltAcc := LTIME#0ms;\nEND_IF;"
  }
]
